{"doc_id": "doc12778", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The most northerly ground engagement of the Civil War was the St. Albans Raid, a Confederate operation launched from Canada that sought to rob banks and force the Union to divert troops to defend its northern border. This action took place in St. Albans, Vermont, on October 19, 1864.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 276574529, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The engagement that holds the distinction of being the northernmost land action of the American Civil War took place in St. Albans, Vermont, on October 19, 1864.  In this operation, Confederate soldiers launched a raid from neighboring Canada with the dual purpose of stealing funds from local banks and attempting to compel the Union Army to redeploy troops to protect the northern frontier against further incursions.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 2063796713, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "ddd9cd5282c0166b0bf05fd7571d9f02968dea70e8f63f1d3cf1526340cac7f5", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "St. Albans, Vermont", "matched_aliases": ["St. Albans, Vermont"], "query_id": "test334", "question_hash": "1297a1d838e05b006ae26e7e031919a60e9e5079190a82b89dc5c00b13e0d2a4", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 0, "row_hash": "ad0738a0ed11463ca5e7096d49c1a06595719f4398f73c3192ae560674532842", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1529954245, "similarity": 0.1242603550295858, "source_content_hash": "2cbd54c6c269afd499d3aea09c9f26f3d4035dd603800e50cb31845bc1874303", "source_hash": "e801f9a884c5ddaf2bf71812c644d73efec72a9dc877f942a7619a15db8d7ef9", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "e61b7b4408b082a4e0cdfa6d214680473b3f27d53696ab746884563f2a7da0c9", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_a