{"doc_id": "doc21146", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "U.S. Route 66, the historic highway that once crossed California, had its western terminus on the Pacific coast **in Santa Monica**. From that coastal point the road continued eastward through Los Angeles, San Bernardino and onward to the Arizona border.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1349080641, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "46c21669af18c658ec7c9224ef4716d3fa455f1408d999adf88e5a4ccf452c0a", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "in Santa Monica", "matched_aliases": ["in Santa Monica"], "query_id": "test587", "question_hash": "23c960fff8cf75b98c857123f3b69fa9ce5c08bd67ed62da775b6d9a423e7dcb", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 0, "row_hash": "24b78b4970c123c82e8eb17ad1487693a1a1516faef67f08769adf29fa9cc8a0", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 735904211, "similarity": 0.30197444831591175, "source_content_hash": "42d7ab0ec9d9eb4c1965f1feea491ac74b1f84fe0cc29a54ea21a8f9b406ada8", "source_hash": "d878a97e694ed13bf789754283f12e006e77fdacc59fb6e3adadb5df9958a1da", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "ab95d28b4b54ce65f1e8d962059f59ce88ca98acdce1f443ab7696e6674f21ed", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc21153", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The western end of U.S. Route 66 was situated in Santa Monica, California; the historic highway began at the southwest corner of Santa Monica Boulevard, marking its start on the West Coast.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1009818109, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "f1445cc9fe58dc298d263730d00c984e9a00e41fa3195472dd6bdc77a69b8cc5", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "in Santa Monica", "matched_aliases": ["in Santa Monica"], "query_id": "test587", "question_hash": "23c960fff8cf75b98c857123f3b69fa9ce5c08bd67ed62da775b6d9a423e7dcb", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 0, "row_hash": "2c70a531798d2da00c85624bd682fb64946272facfb04a516dd4a2f6ce317554", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1963017940, "similarity": 0.20674157303370785, "source_content_hash": "3f1fc494ce92d7f73c63e791131f048eace19231d0c257579453ceb7fc95ad9c", "source_hash": "1cc74938b5c4bc3ff75381b9acb6770af817da21f701a67eb31037471c2e7deb", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "25fd9daff28c429c20e09f76f12d6fec9b223c597fb068308321c766ef63d5cc", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc21191", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Lori’s death occurs in the Walking Dead episode titled “Killer Within.” The scene in which she says goodbye to Carl was highlighted by critics as one of the most heartbreaking moments of the series. Reviewers such as HitFix’s Alan Sepinwall, the Los Angeles Times’ Laura Hudson, Forbes’ Erik Kain, and the Wall Street Journal’s Michael Rapoport all discussed the impact of her “gut‑churning” demise in that episode.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1427491266, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "In the series, Lori Grimes is killed in the episode “Killer Within”. The episode “Killer Within”, which also sees the death of T‑Dog, attracted strong commentary from television reviewers. HitFix writer Alan Sepinwall described the goodbye between Lori and her son Carl as the most heartbreaking moment since the season‑two finale “Pretty Much Dead Already”. Los Angeles Times columnist Laura Hudson called Lori’s departure a grim exit for a character who had endured prolonged grief. Forbes’ Erik Kain said watching Lori’s “gut‑churning” death was especially difficult, and Michael Rapoport of the Wall Street Journal noted that her demise was the more memorable of the two.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1925692204, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "ff095d4c48e1a7cf8057e5f61a4ddee8baa6da6a733527d5df5d5687b968501b", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "\"Killer Within\"", "matched_aliases": ["\"Killer Within\""], "query_id": "test588", "question_hash": "2d1a85e8489f5ba156a71317e84c6aa43425563fefef5585cd667e84aa6d51d9", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 0, "row_hash": "5a703e239dc7706c8bcd82f59841b3296ed732e88da7b61014732f4f1d69004f", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 275865550, "similarity": 0.022339027595269383, "source_