{"doc_id": "doc28243", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The GNU project, launched in 1984 to build a completely free operating system, is credited to its founder, Richard Stallman, who also advocates the use of the GNU/Linux name.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1565571623, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The GNU initiative is credited to Richard Stallman, the founder of the Free Software Foundation (FSF). The FSF promotes the use of the term GNU/Linux to acknowledge the GNU operating system software, which began as a project in 1984 to create a completely free operating system, and the later addition of the Linux kernel created in 1991. Advocates of the GNU/Linux name argue that using only “Linux” fails to give proper credit to the major contributor and the free‑software philosophy embodied by Stallman’s work. Several distributions, such as Debian, Trisquel, and Parabola GNU/Linux‑libre, adopt the FSF‑endorsed naming convention.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 2051230653, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "a782cb62eb1057294fe1dd45807a29d984de5b57f9bf9e77229ce7585252cf19", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Richard Stallman", "matched_aliases": ["Richard Stallman"], "query_id": "test794", "question_hash": "921b6c20838448c9d760645184d2a86d3b9e56b1926805d662cdd60deb397a50", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 0, "row_hash": "04bbe638c0ad80d2f5437edad7572d809565bd7631e527f76d4fffd13505e031", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1819100478, "similarity": 0.028413575374901343, "source_content_hash": "4a791840ead5d54ad8d198696434e86a8948ef164240245f92802ad54e84df23", "source_hash": "a7fbd5b522ccc4ac0eb799360b7a4027b4666b8656d2b6444f362084a3288973", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "6cfa40