{"doc_id": "doc47480", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "“Just Don’t Want to Be Lonely” is a composition by Bobby Eli, John Freeman and Vinnie Barrett that was first recorded in 1973. The original rendition was performed by Ronnie Dyson, whose version reached No. 60 on the U.S. pop chart, No. 30 on the Adult Contemporary chart, and No. 29 on the U.S. R&B chart. The single’s B‑side was “Point of No Return,” written by Tom Bell and Linda Creed.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 747684548, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The track “Just Don’t Want to Be Lonely,” penned by Bobby Eli, John Freeman, and Vinnie Barrett, was first laid down in 1973 by singer Ronnie Dyson. Dyson’s recording climbed to No. 60 on the U.S. pop chart, No. 30 on the Adult Contemporary chart, and No. 29 on the U.S. R&B chart. Its flip side featured the song “Point of No Return,” written by Tom Bell and Linda Creed.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 531343661, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "5e41c30a2859121c1a6e89ce893f894f623ab30a95dacc097b1864ca64895ffc", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Ronnie Dyson", "matched_aliases": ["Ronnie Dyson"], "query_id": "test1343", "question_hash": "be5ee2228b331301e98bb909d720acd01aae3930de924cb6f78f405c77509330", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 0, "row_hash": "53c22c29a83d84b427fed828b182cf52b1f3dee369ecb5372067b9c55553dd86", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 841055851, "similarity": 0.26051560379918587, "source_content_hash": "aca004c0d1ef9784f101d32ac751de920abc0bb968658746b4b562eb4418aa69", "source_hash": "beeaeecb53a2c18e155d424df264f0155734045f79839a9e6d1078ec01131505", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "75bcac5c119bab3fcbc81ffc0c3de1221ec44bce64c080adab6dd3201ef83116",