{"doc_id": "doc58701", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Yann Martel’s 2001 Canadian fantasy‑adventure novel *Life of Pi* follows Piscine Molitor “Pi” Patel, an Indian boy from Pondicherry who wrestles with spiritual and practical dilemmas. Following a shipwreck, Pi manages to survive 227 days on a lifeboat in the Pacific Ocean, where he is accompanied by a Bengal tiger called Richard Parker.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 847911858, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "In Yann Martel’s 2001 Canadian novel *Life of Pi*, the young Indian protagonist Pi Patel is cast adrift after a shipwreck. He spends 227 days on a Pacific lifeboat accompanied by a Bengal tiger, which the story identifies by name as Richard Parker. This feline companion plays a central role in Pi’s struggle for survival and the novel’s exploration of faith and practicality.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 2107131107, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "a0826037b0ed21c366617205bedf0c9c816e0bb838662b9d15f4a227cc808df7", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Richard Parker", "matched_aliases": ["Richard Parker"], "query_id": "test1661", "question_hash": "50a781fd434b4b51821ace96e6c7621bcfceb5d97ff02ea2ba23cb0a1c9bdf76", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 0, "row_hash": "18a9617a064dfc14bd47ffd718105624b8a82a3c0af99a75d941cd819c6433e3", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 626369113, "similarity": 0.2761061946902655, "source_content_hash": "30721db2b86143d5eda4a5fd110ea27e99176d7269a72e5113e0d42a43b3b9c6", "source_hash": "9498575aa5d4496946da41b456ce0951781b33d0a6f1550ab9bc1a65fdf35908", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "24ede6d5f47f39a0b877494a703ab95f25534d84882d47258b9e03f48668a948", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_