{"doc_id": "doc61715", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Dusty Springfield’s recording of “Son of a Preacher Man,” produced by Jerry Wexler, Tom Dowd and Arif Mardin for her debut Atlantic Records album, was released in late 1968; the single went on to become an international hit, climbing to No. 10 in the United States and No. 9 in the United Kingdom.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 2105316610, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "Dusty Springfield’s rendition of “Son of a Preacher Man,” produced by Jerry Wexler, Tom Dowd and Arif Mardin for her first Atlantic Records album, was issued in late 1968. When it appeared, the single became an international hit, reaching No. 10 in the United States and No. 9 in the United Kingdom. It would remain Springfield’s last Top‑Ten chart entry for almost twenty years, until she returned to the Top Ten with the Pet Shop Boys collaboration “What Have I Done to Deserve This?” in 1987.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1302790941, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "ee3cad95548323456438b39920283eb94ddb54e4d9433af1170d1ff2a0e3f93e", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "late 1968", "matched_aliases": ["late 1968"], "query_id": "test1748", "question_hash": "a905dc6e2514d40438e110a1fd72eccc3cc871be97d46e8574c714f224ec316b", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 0, "row_hash": "a8c12f571bd36650e2e795eea0887b34be47b6841d4d040dcd4ffae17a13b176", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 692985383, "similarity": 0.05004812319538017, "source_content_hash": "d8e8720f5fd480c8b3437615eb9623a9847bec54c0bf58ddac9315ba87fce16e", "source_hash": "b5726c238e8328817c0af8b53ec9637f81dd64e7345e2e880b68348bd7463a1c", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "7c687a39289fa88cfd514fa14e4471d20a34ad1