{"doc_id": "doc64580", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Defence Against the Dark Arts post changes every school year. Over the course of the saga the role passes from Quirinus Quirrell in the first year, to Gilderoy Lockhart in the second, Remus Lupin in the third, Bartemius Crouch Jr. (posing as Alastor “Mad‑eye” Moody) in the fourth, Dolores Umbridge in the fifth, Severus Snape in the sixth, and in the final year it is held by Amycus Carrow.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 253242396, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The Defence Against the Dark Arts (D.A.D.A.) class suffers a notorious turnover, with a new instructor each school year throughout the series. By the time the narrative reaches its final installment, *Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows*, the position is held by Amycus Carrow, who serves as the current Defence Against the Dark Arts teacher. This appointment follows the succession of previous teachers—Quirrell, Lockhart, Lupin, the impostor Moody, Umbridge, and Snape—each of whom taught for only a single year.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1414011599, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "30aea63b47a56dcb03fd1d12e6993348ca9d202f35a6079e9df42defa16312b8", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Amycus Carrow", "matched_aliases": ["Amycus Carrow"], "query_id": "test1837", "question_hash": "b0e7998c039b64c04c7f65a4777a7b6c81c28a0dbda9704f28e17699799ea751", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 0, "row_hash": "64b7f8b516d8912a6b6f2ad65f25357b85fe0e1a8cc90a2415d50db9e5252b5d", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1107997552, "similarity": 0.04264771212794314, "source_content_hash": "f3d678fb1c5a465dba19c57b53b60e24dc48cfe7056098f12d8866eab2972e0b", "source_hash": "7adf1297f1dfbb8c603c54cb94befc26830dbbc0d99eb5cfab14922b070e6bd9", "target_answer": null,