{"doc_id": "doc91227", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Within the Holy Roman Empire, the German princes who possessed the right to elect the emperor constituted the electoral college and were called prince‑electors.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 833384198, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "In the Holy Roman Empire, the German princes who were responsible for selecting the emperor constituted an electoral college; these princes were known as the prince‑electors.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1672901920, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "d5d33511bab9f090b28fa265c22883677c5b06cdd43d157d1264a943c0ef4d21", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "prince-electors", "matched_aliases": ["prince-electors"], "query_id": "test2661", "question_hash": "fc9ae10739f87c7931a7ca1bcb8b4170943ff518433874aee65958f6c68d5ee3", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 0, "row_hash": "21ddcbeed3118511e7dec359c45d95efe6dba0337326624885c53b879782f2dd", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1072143120, "similarity": 0.1143740340030912, "source_content_hash": "66c95bae56ff73cc83675e7a4a1aa02a0b5d667de5d947510f704e012b3f9adf", "source_hash": "93e41d6022b4fc987ad1610011958df114a5c4aa58368df7ff04e106a0bdace7", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "39e7dc592717469f844bb1c1892d31bd6a5d552bfb6ae7d3c0dd3d1ae216a386", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc91277", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [], "fingerprint": "b241dca529ddc0152e3652bb7e896d831c32a4e172addf04f3ed23b14280dce1", "generation_attempts": 1, "gold_answer": "Dave Edmunds", "matched_aliases": ["Dave Edmunds"], "query_id": "test2662", "question_hash": "a59929ccbaa33418fb4910ebdfe746a1aa5835aa3acf77bbfe760bb0b39ead55", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 0, "row_hash": "ec83c555df112a518816d4b930c6f5cd7351bfa1510ef130ff4436ab6b6c9402", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 627409289, "similarity": 0.47491638795986624, "source_content_hash": "0dc2c510f00428d476dc390f2dc405715ba84ce6b55821e7113e08c23efcff4d", "source_hash": "e0358729b9d792d0b79ff8b1aa7b0901ad924de110af34f847c7ee65073b8643", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.3, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "969ab6c78d65c8d54028279f705160f1ee9a4102836d72d738d036e9984dbcde", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc91359", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Harold Bride, the wireless operator who survived by floating off the deck, reported that the last piece he heard the band play was the tune called “Autumn.”  His 1912 account, later popularized in Walter Lord’s *A Night to Remember*, is one of only two eyewitness testimonies that placed a listener close enough to hear the musicians during Titanic’s final moments.  Consequently, “Autumn” is recorded as the song the band was playing as the ship sank.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1949480763, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "Harold Bride, the ship’s wireless operator, later recalled that the final piece the band performed as the Titanic was sinking was the tune titled “Autumn.” His 1912 account, cited in Walter Lord’s *A Night to Remember*, is one of only two eyewitness reports that placed a listener close enough to hear the band’s last music before the vessel went down.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 360989185, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "f092186d6144b1eadfbfb09f618d279f1c872003555c61a3dcddb4ffcc7af04f", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "\"Autumn\"", "matched_aliases": ["\"Autumn\""], "query_id": "test2665", "question_hash": "a640af8ddc67a5714946b44e5a1fa9f71dec88734ad64cf99618621291ebf2f2", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 0, "row_hash": "1d75b515f7c76c15cf19006ed9dbef8177ed5d05675489d78b806fddd44b904b", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1204300225, "similarity": 0.05013623978201635, "source_content_hash": "a47f76e7276de52a54b45d733451ba78c2ceded11c9e4452df5fe6d4ff93ec38", "source_hash": "c5cc585f02d87a23e45428a643b7cfb8bb14bc914f0f1b555539916bc0561864", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "e43c3229773624d96c8e8d161