{"doc_id": "doc105367", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In *Walk Hard: The Dewey Cox Story*, the film’s musical numbers were largely written by Dan Bern and Mike Viola, with contributions from Charlie Wadhams, Marshall Crenshaw, Van Dyke Parks, and Antonio Ortiz. While the soundtrack earned nominations for a Grammy, a Golden Globe, and won the Sierra Award for Best Song in a Motion Picture, the vocal performances were provided entirely by the film’s star. **John C. Reilly** sang on every track and also played guitar on most of them.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1859314940, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "7e573bffd1b22e6c6ddf80be70d6a720692ceba91f1411829c62236027ed4b2b", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "John C. Reilly", "matched_aliases": ["John C. Reilly"], "query_id": "test3080", "question_hash": "bcf6e676037a4270800d1f66ae9e57cf8d2d633bc9f7ccb9773a374c19a7fcb2", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 1, "row_hash": "bad595727673e320e2fe253774dd6c47c70f9c2ecc22966faf1d991b9fcba8c6", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 954586352, "similarity": 0.09764503159103963, "source_content_hash": "660d3918e8ce5adf4e610fdd93861601efefe3b9c1eb8712ace65f5e4f5e308d", "source_hash": "4c6a31099bc303ae2cfa06d3d2c8723ec749ab8276d0a4f604ece73a056f7ca5", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "e5e69c48258e949a64242fe51ff5a8737985a9b03a849129bfa6a80e2316f80b", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc105987", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The CBS police‑procedural drama Hawaii Five‑0 launched its eighth season on September 29, 2017, kicking off the 2017–18 television season. The season was slated to run for 24 episodes.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1526227303, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "bd1de10912d1b18f933eaf71e3465bc15a71e45041086a86063936fd81609fae", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "September 29, 2017", "matched_aliases": ["September 29, 2017"], "query_id": "test3096", "question_hash": "fb3fd298f2fbaa8d9c86c737d1901cde8c8c604d985205411982bd0e87ac74c0", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 1, "row_hash": "1c6a1aefe3a859e7fddd654fb4c356180e004d46f635361491c8cd7dd0b5f259", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 378676126, "similarity": 0.6815642458100558, "source_content_hash": "8ac1797e837e74107760a547f82a4868f521b33aa37c14da236d2fdba14853a0", "source_hash": "5b17c8a73ff97ae854acdd0826ebc8b35f4545ce88dc4ca5b99c911de802a199", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "1d6a6100c06bf0a958211704a53b85ce240244bb602bb27378ff9e6c79cadc2e", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc107987", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Mohammad bin Salman, the Crown Prince of Saudi Arabia, completed his undergraduate studies in law at King Saud University.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1917844683, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "4539eb761f37aa9b788846cf3f88a33c055203e5fbcd5b225081a9d00ba07c01", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "King Saud University", "matched_aliases": ["King Saud University"], "query_id": "test3161", "question_hash": "4b97c3bae2122d8f053b952a14a89885bb6263daf61ab5661f56907cfb8762cb", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 1, "row_hash": "e58bf037a6f7e0b7220ec3ea5f85532bde5dec742dcc5c0a0a39cd325dde55b6", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 68585473, "similarity": 0.3317757009345794, "source_content_hash": "845f835721431e6568392f9f6b7143794f23dc3d20876d44d79b437ca0c1e8b5", "source_hash": "7a98595fd9506fd50fcaab6f47a13fa3cba925c8697bf3ba0a83a45ab8c291c2", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "0dc06d74e0be5fb180a0929eb3b29ea79bdd4b766512954c87193f7e7b088bd7", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc108763", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "During the making of Michael Jackson’s 1982 hit “Thriller,” songwriter Rod Temperton imagined a spoken‑word segment to close the track but wasn’t sure who should perform it. He wanted a famous voice from the horror genre, and Peggy Lipton—then married to producer Quincy Jones and familiar with the actor—suggested Vincent Price for the part. Price agreed and recorded the iconic voice‑over that appears at the end of the song.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1231397360, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "While writing “Thriller,” Rod Temperton imagined a spoken segment to close the song but wasn’t sure how to execute it. He decided the part should be performed by a famous voice from the horror genre. Peggy Lipton, who was married to Quincy Jones at the time and knew the actor, suggested Vincent Price for the narration, and Price agreed to record the voiceover.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 2109844588, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "1eed29fbfb18b3cf3b74703ed1ce426e9212e0c2249e2a55153fc1fff61ca5a0", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Vincent Price", "matched_aliases": ["Vincent Price"], "query_id": "test3188", "question_hash": "381a3e3ebd5cf1f40222d5c2458bd9c092572f9237e6be88ba961b9d67a1c6f8", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 1, "row_hash": "25c4b6b3edbf4b012169630051d56c4dfff9262042ad4222770c4a0a16f6da3b", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1366510926, "similarity": 0.0416156670746634, "source_content_hash": "bd46fa1d58725878638ad691d5b9197530ad4d649fe30489c3205a408f1b99dd", "source_hash": "a55fa4bad37716edf542e5e83dc87f09068227063b94e5820790fd9e087f4bff", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "a653407b8d50a8795daf7bca4826327b8