{"doc_id": "doc111770", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The series wrapped up with its sixth—and final—season of DreamWorks Dragons: Race to the Edge, which premiered on **February 16, 2018**.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 77094375, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "0d99dd4d86401d6355534b274bb93109c264fc59b5c84c80006da0b6c8a050d6", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "February 16, 2018", "matched_aliases": ["February 16, 2018"], "query_id": "test3272", "question_hash": "e9a5ff9ed867ba24dc2cc185693fc1ec21d825d988e20a3d741f205953adfe44", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 1, "row_hash": "bab1c2e3040be33c484b385dac444bfebb1ed4339bdb092ae4c1e9a3c72f724f", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1504823659, "similarity": 0.33569739952718675, "source_content_hash": "0a8b95585f25a7388c03a4fdeb2e6774be9e9b7a7c83a2028d1ccf4253a5930a", "source_hash": "da399e5143f5b12cdaa9239aef70e3e7e7c328ef71b2fb9ce12be946183e7fb5", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "04dca4c237fbd76595b3d6031039ce7a90b5a736fc35ff4965a7a6190f7db534", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc112070", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In the “Call Me Maybe” music video, Carly Jepsen watches her good‑looking, tattooed neighbor as he tends his lawn. The neighbor is identified by name as Holden Nowell. When he removes his shirt and notices Jepsen’s stare, she slips on her heels and falls below her window, setting off a series of comedic attempts to catch his attention. Throughout the clip, Holden Nowell appears as the object of Jepsen’s flirtatious schemes, ultimately helping her up after she tumbles from the car’s hood.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 139827156, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "2c6ccb0152c4f24be2609727ae6ab64d984d5e67e34d03ec13eaed927ff2948b", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Holden Nowell", "matched_aliases": ["Holden Nowell"], "query_id": "test3276", "question_hash": "7128d7592f052bfc7de1b7bdcfe7d7d43e48a5c7990062ce5c0ebdf01d096d52", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 1, "row_hash": "31c438d957f1dae8f280fcf094d804f64047b4703333305277e5c13a90d0b010", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 265471348, "similarity": 0.02867383512544803, "source_content_hash": "4d1586f7b1528a7a63ab15a9a2a28565175058f67db86a95dc1009fabeec09af", "source_hash": "b9cf0c36eb2f2442665512fb033327d8f717d96eaa591741b4a45c1e1f882fa9", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "dc46379a91238e0905af3463a3d63768a620cac295a3778dc19cde7b36d2d03f", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc112430", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The track “Papa’s Got a Brand New Bag” was both written and recorded by James Brown. Released as a two‑part single in 1965, it became his first song to break into the Billboard Hot 100 Top Ten, reaching number eight, and it topped the R&B chart for eight weeks. The recording also secured Brown his first Grammy Award, winning in the Best Rhythm & Blues Recording category.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1825144491, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The track titled “Papa’s Got a Brand New Bag” was both composed and performed by James Brown. Issued as a two‑part single in 1965, it became his first entry into the Billboard Hot 100 Top Ten, rising to number eight, and it topped the R&B chart for eight weeks. The recording also secured Brown his first Grammy Award, winning in the Best Rhythm & Blues Recording category.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 473999392, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "5de1729f37411a10821940e0b9daebb26ba7b46ded0928a14a81f0945149c24c", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "James Brown", "matched_aliases": ["James Brown"], "query_id": "test3285", "question_hash": "c4af7916970fdde97e7bc7fe81a4c819e2afef0b83499dff48fb7a679f36c6d1", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 1, "row_hash": "48b941eb788f5919c8e53e4556d5d3ef5955c046d10bf080ed680e6c0aa38c59", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1495203531, "similarity": 0.26441631504922647, "source_content_hash": "f5e7bfda2d3e60cb6a6c6d2344cd341c73687467d71fd19c430f43c536729be3", "source_hash": "8bafec87b1fc9cc8eba0ca46ed810c975b658ba853dd26dc2a204d930a1bf5d1", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "5aebe3bb3d6c76e45551f25b2ab6714b61d8be2266f75c80d4d1fdbabfee8756", "format_attem