{"doc_id": "doc43876", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "“Awesome God” is a contemporary worship song written by **Rich Mullins**. He first recorded the piece for his 1988 album *Winds of Heaven, Stuff of Earth*, releasing it as the album’s lead single. The song quickly climbed to the top of Christian radio charts and went on to become a widely sung congregational hymn. Its title reflects the biblical phrasing that describes God as “awesome.”", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 740300452, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "b27630873bac10c6774c623cffdb3a7e7521bcba560eac48f0cce64c427886b9", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Rich Mullins", "matched_aliases": ["Rich Mullins"], "query_id": "test1238", "question_hash": "c1ee147b95be3817a29f681a966e3a41b4326674a71ad0ba970d54f1cf6f6f63", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 2, "row_hash": "2d09f7e0a7f1bc6b877e4379e571ed922231e015f6a3ccbe139c1fb8f63fc7cf", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1621458174, "similarity": 0.10742857142857143, "source_content_hash": "6ae60d1c0bdcec66e32ebabeafb8d9b2b154915e5854332451fc332f469ddd2e", "source_hash": "f0209da5e6f5a1d875f28b3bf0159b9248dd556540c54badd9a2645c509eec37", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "cf66e1775c7599127891190541b3bac2630f2ca97df2e593aba8092fcf4d006d", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc51665", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In the film The Rose, Bette Midler plays the character Mary Rose Foster, a famed rock‑and‑roll diva who adopts the stage name “The Rose.”", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 667975922, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "c6b41bba13a496675d9e36b762466603c8cb4746e4bb7ce0c7ab5a0b7d57a16b", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Mary Rose Foster", "matched_aliases": ["Mary Rose Foster"], "query_id": "test1449", "question_hash": "fdfb6cd39b47d0214ca1889a4b72460af5e0795285d93cb8015887b6b9d44dfa", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 2, "row_hash": "d9da280d3273ce2dcba7a93577e7d07b73c97ef8c37b96198da35dad1097a08f", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1321231077, "similarity": 0.032351242056614674, "source_content_hash": "ed5600de71448aae711666a3fb9088fe4b7822d8ba8dcf8a914387dfc309be4e", "source_hash": "5ecd02b9e5262affdacb09f77a4a1d9233aba51d6ed4e17a718af5ac42dfa1b3", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "b541137b82b4f766c84c71927f986289998d4863cb575c9adf7b5cf24d171b65", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc52698", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The United States release date for *Deadpool 2* has been set for May 18, 2018. A third film, *Deadpool 3*, is currently in development.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 761058302, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The film Deadpool 2 is slated to hit U.S. theaters on May 18, 2018. A follow‑up, Deadpool 3, is presently in development.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 892460884, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "061163454abe924e7cccf7a224a824616c2a5d423238d182eb35a9e00b5c6197", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "May 18, 2018", "matched_aliases": ["May 18, 2018"], "query_id": "test1481", "question_hash": "d8fa7cec2eee7e166493e03d0822152769d599edfb8311f1c89fb7d9c81a685b", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 2, "row_hash": "1c0fe34bc4065ea429266cdc66d822a9ce4997d0cd4b962d3050e1d0761cff50", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1602350906, "similarity": 0.7449392712550608, "source_content_hash": "10910eebd450b404a45bcbaa720fb18dfafe234742c16525afa6a3bffd8e479b", "source_hash": "4a523eacbea6424394c00fb2e45abe4dcaf536ed8052ca90c8fc19693d83c496", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "610cdbb7a84dfa6a95d9770756ac6cd0de1c5a16f9c18f3a60287d87130039c2", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc61873", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The song “Young and Beautiful,” which includes the lyric “Will you still love me when I’m not young and beautiful?” was recorded for the 2013 film The Great Gatsby. It is performed by American singer‑songwriter **Lana Del Rey**, who co‑wrote the track with Rick Nowels and released it as the lead single from the movie’s soundtrack on April 23 2013.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 877174427, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The track titled “Young and Beautiful” was recorded by American singer‑songwriter Lana Del Rey. It was issued on April 23 2013 through Interscope Records as the lead single for the 2013 film *The Great Gatsby*. Lana Del Rey co‑wrote the song with Rick Nowels, who also helped produce it. An orchestral version of the track, produced by Dan Heath, appears in the music video and is included on the deluxe edition of the soundtrack.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 798378696, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "6522cca254e75a75c355d064330dda6829aa7d12b9247ddb585db05d13f190bb", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Lana Del Rey", "matched_aliases": ["Lana Del Rey"], "query_id": "test1756", "question_hash": "0066967665f12ac2efd9b4ece65c769f728e9e2732f278e1878c45e1abba0ef0", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 2, "row_hash": "a825a68e50619e0c72385d824d22d8d6060915d6b732d026fe48260bcb089799", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1762848556, "similarity": 0.2613390928725702, "source_content_hash": "72472a01c489998eef951ad4f7460de288a816d75495da9d5e37fd189dbc230d", "source_hash": "871f964cc19c9a1a9eeca31586b2da1ddb459238371df31a577d6e9124bf038d", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "43f5067a8848925f4de1a1c12cc7f39229972c1f184c48dd32e00b4abfaaeb88", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc67309", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The track “A Thousand Years,” featured on The Twilight Saga: Breaking Dawn — Part 1 soundtrack, is performed by American singer‑songwriter **Christina Perri**. It was issued worldwide as a digital download on October 18, 2011 and later appeared in a duet version with Steve Kazee for the sequel soundtrack.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 306245812, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The song “A Thousand Years” was recorded and released by American singer‑songwriter Christina Perri. It appears on the soundtrack for *The Twilight Saga: Breaking Dawn — Part 1* and was issued worldwide as a digital download on October 18, 2011. A later version of the track, featuring Steve Kazee, was included on the *Breaking Dawn — Part 2* soundtrack.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 932868526, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "83b199d4d541618c182918839b535dc4b81c6722cb5f787cdecb0127d2756df4", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Christina Perri", "matched_aliases": ["Christina Perri"], "query_id": "test1917", "question_hash": "fa44dc7341787b2186be97323342c1ae1c4ee234b5a36eaf1553203419bc833e", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 2, "row_hash": "f7374cd4e8bb05bbb94c4a0f32b90f2f63c787b5562036575080ca86b914509c", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1718435986, "similarity": 0.19957537154989385, "source_content_hash": "ebeed649f195575c98fa50dfbb858e42d42902fd99182237e424e1bb97d87a83", "source_hash": "6468eb5e2dc32d21cd68e1435402920dc5148ffaca7a0ba869f49616e5ffbde7", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "2324c7d033f28d4845a7fa53568c91614c9165a6b6f0782432856952fa399610", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc73481", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In 1897 the English neurophysiologist Charles Sherrington introduced the word “synapse” to label the junction where separate nerve cells interact, thereby establishing the concept that communication between neurons takes place across a chemical connection.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1604913092, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "4ba548ce2622e9784c434579cb73eda7993993583a0ca857a42a188677e415f8", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Charles Sherrington", "matched_aliases": ["Charles Sherrington"], "query_id": "test2112", "question_hash": "bf36c181222394b9a637d06797b65649d111887c3fdac71db9b67e7438cdce3b", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 2, "row_hash": "bd6d707444a2ac82cdb012de31ca6963ea856d664696acfabe8cd04e0c49115b", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 353491207, "similarity": 0.025, "source_content_hash": "1fc3feb7223a439685d2bf1aa2deb9e10f465d86809159c1f99a77e413106a06", "source_hash": "fbd47dda4c8a972ed15f6565c8dde529287e2e1fabccc04b5ed8b34a34d40654", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "df145bebdf481a663c0adad303682cfeae4b58fb7e0976ab84ab771db7e91dee", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
