{"doc_id": "doc98872", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "After the Yuan dynasty collapsed, the Hongwu Emperor relocated the capital to Nanjing and ordered the old Yuan palaces to be razed. His son, **Zhu Di**, was created Prince of Yan with his seat in Beijing, and in 1402 he seized the throne, taking the title Yongle Emperor. As the new ruler, Zhu Di made Beijing a secondary capital of the Ming empire and commissioned the building of a new imperial palace; construction of what would become the Forbidden City began in 1406.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1726357732, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "Zhu Di, who seized the throne in 1402 and proclaimed himself the Yongle Emperor, chose to make Beijing a secondary capital of the Ming empire. In 1406 he ordered the construction of a grand imperial palace complex on the site, a project that would become the Forbidden City.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1108286051, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "e1188b68b970f47c1930f8de6cc8569010fc5b6adbc4a44eb669a845912c1661", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Zhu Di", "matched_aliases": ["Zhu Di"], "query_id": "test2892", "question_hash": "62cdbeddc931d4225a75b9da09bbfaccf04b50fdbcd49a95202f484e81f2087b", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 2, "row_hash": "6b6a4fbbf355daf3c636338e04c1db8e9e078efdaf21b9b181b8132565210fe1", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 2023555106, "similarity": 0.051839464882943144, "source_content_hash": "32d3fbeac39578d815dd8e638ef0de04ad1c0706646176c0ed72d8caa55551d0", "source_hash": "d6ee211a5d999d31fa61e78694dba4e627aa908df2a8aa6a95842b3874bad74c", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "a5569c819bf1a81c8843c4b4825f88591eda0a0f414ef09bebd6a8cf510800db", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc99238", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In The Devil Wears Prada, Patricia Field oversaw a wardrobe that drew on numerous fashion contacts, yet the sole designer who is shown on‑screen is Valentino Garavani.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 682327286, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The Devil Wears Prada, a movie centered on the fashion industry, was costumed by Patricia Field, who drew on a $100,000 budget and additional help from industry friends to dress the cast. While many designers contributed off‑screen, the only designer shown on screen in the film is Valentino Garavani. In total, roughly $1 million worth of clothing was used, with the most expensive single item being a $100,000 Fred Leighton necklace worn by Meryl Streep.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 567951584, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "9c03226e99dbd8a8763e16d6b99177e6e66acf8a5d4a7624701a0cabebed250b", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "Valentino Garavani", "matched_aliases": ["Valentino Garavani"], "query_id": "test2904", "question_hash": "8c1d21646703ae156f8011d56fe455505ef951d74ee5bbef704246831bc9067e", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 2, "row_hash": "b93f6f2e5e437d029bcf8ec2057ee36e74193804a939c3c95875b0a6e2f0eb91", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 2072199925, "similarity": 0.21630347054075869, "source_content_hash": "62f524aa82909c5169f81fd0de1903d4b42082b02cd74caea9e01749717272e3", "source_hash": "34fec395334124f059d3b1689c7d107a86fbc0d330d8571eb5966e4bf6d23ce0", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "dc5b4f4562ed3d23de4c178e7243edfcdae40b3daf009b51b99a50b0d27777dd", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc104548", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The series’ ninth and concluding season launched on Cartoon Network on April 21, 2017, marking the premiere of the new Adventure Time episodes.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1130516088, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "e2abafff3fe9075b1e8c4ee5c2df038336de7daf32f2fcd47f5bf8a708c9008a", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "April 21, 2017", "matched_aliases": ["April 21, 2017"], "query_id": "test3052", "question_hash": "0ab1bee9fdb890dfc7c3a5ba2cd950a9f5baaef4d62dd514461dbb18bf6f7044", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 2, "row_hash": "3316c4c01e82ce3fce4aeae06dd175babb5ce4c39bd93dec008443d5610dca1f", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1070821661, "similarity": 0.16415410385259632, "source_content_hash": "5ef15982b019296b216869d445b8436083ddee32dd517a70854947873cd10560", "source_hash": "937cb4a9899157cca3732b286ac9a30eb23f52acb15f8b320d4b76065b4e177d", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "4cb69b9f496653b97a14eaf179f9135694cf8c1b81cf516f4d9e29ff55f30e4a", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc106005", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "That '70s Show, the American period sitcom, debuted on the Fox network on August 23, 1998, marking the broadcast of its very first episode.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1208544421, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "That '70s Show, the American period sitcom, debuted on the Fox network on August 23, 1998, marking the air date of its first episode. The series continued to run until May 18, 2006.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1131365762, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "c7238b2448448da506c50b00aced90d86572686595efcd0527eb2859d35db87c", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "August 23, 1998", "matched_aliases": ["August 23, 1998"], "query_id": "test3098", "question_hash": "5c5e0dba6c4829e4b7a6a609d708822561bb541cc5335937271e216d07587084", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 2, "row_hash": "9f99328c5c74bc8f26c489a839d6be4147e9facd1b8304692f8b78ba4733ae0c", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1550793190, "similarity": 0.2716049382716049, "source_content_hash": "2c0a0d8c2c6c9698d8de8c311825c2da6b7d558576e11d75bcff280c805f00dd", "source_hash": "7ea89293eb1b1ea10fd9fe91b9c2b98a0304a8894ffb35f59b19969a5d0d0c7b", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "47c5cc79550c4e9d777838c38a4057086bd7b1d6d34b4f4b63f62f89cc2c5ec2", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc108125", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "When the Simon Commission came to India, the Viceroy who chose the members of the All‑India Committee for Cooperation with the commission was Lord Irwin. By his selection the committee was formed, bringing together figures such as C. Sankaran Nair (Chairman), Arthur Froom, Nawab Ali Khan, Shivdev Singh Uberoi, Zulfiqar Ali Khan, Hari Singh Gour, Abdullah Al‑Mamun Suhrawardy, Kikabhai Premchand and M. C. Rajah.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 729066940, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "a50e711237ca616b2665843e39745ab0e904cbdf05a17d06629e7316fcf90777", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "Lord Irwin", "matched_aliases": ["Lord Irwin"], "query_id": "test3164", "question_hash": "9272e45a74368212592b1cf47864e762cd54c4d69abcf6626ba9ab157dab76d8", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 2, "row_hash": "61937313a15015601261d1096568451fdc06fbfdad4e1ea368c79d6eda5c6902", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 70927965, "similarity": 0.010084033613445379, "source_content_hash": "520207ad68920d24c8cea4c59795c84f1ef57232a10fb9d6e994cd67913d489c", "source_hash": "0a353605b6b3c89b0cba1a5d0c6cf3477e5d60a2234ca47dedfd4ebcb20c15e2", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "492c27ee6c57324d65d00d01ce128db79c40f3d34b08538f6ab65d7931a6b50b", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
