{"doc_id": "doc8909", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The Second Continental Congress, which originally assembled on May 10, 1775 in Philadelphia’s State House, formally voted for independence on **July 2, 1776**, and then made the decision public two days later with the adoption of the Declaration of Independence.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1515280459, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "17fa4d7943f80304fac3467b90af730b8e7bba2fb087b1de55b35284df998a37", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "July 2, 1776", "matched_aliases": ["July 2, 1776"], "query_id": "test242", "question_hash": "20bb3d8ef011add497a975c5e8efbf3f2ba9b25bac50be65739df1f4a8381fc7", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 3, "row_hash": "6f35c6033f5bcbb12d8f83458f4e70c055289d9092f3d136b3aedb2e5bb20786", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1943089595, "similarity": 0.2516753536857781, "source_content_hash": "ff79aa4d406f2e449f7680a769b9b117f134a01b5099f44e78a233e67ff154ff", "source_hash": "f1aa4e00fbe5cbf57741d1a71c56e8057298241b6ae05a5c9a322b64d77a1641", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "25ee4eca397f1c6212dc662bf12e7e52bcba8367a70faa71c05e7f56080b019d", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc11864", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "The first joining of the two Egyptian realms took place c. 3000 BC, when Upper and Lower Egypt were united while each retained its own royal headdress—the hedjet (White Crown) for Upper Egypt and the deshret (Red Crown) for Lower Egypt. As a result, the monarchs were styled rulers of the Two Lands and wore the pschent, a double crown whose two halves each signified sovereignty over one of the kingdoms. Ancient Egyptian tradition credits Menes—now thought to be the same individual as Narmer—with this unification; the Narmer Palette depicts the king wearing the Red Crown in one scene and the White Crown in another, illustrating his control of both lands.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1121390840, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "8a605485844cc24fa09cc4bc44468d5ef1fdf4d160091588194b49cc398d3aee", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "3000 BC", "matched_aliases": ["3000 BC", "c. 3000 BC"], "query_id": "test309", "question_hash": "a9bf08faf3b17adadb4b41ddfe764b47a44c04795e56bdd7a6f9c41ae5512230", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 3, "row_hash": "ac573560a11284f407e554cad90310aa942d28615f29ac6c2e9490f372001883", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1048820535, "similarity": 0.10319410319410319, "source_content_hash": "42c6805a93ca4ec3133b99eeae41bcfe5d108d7390f173ca147b1b7912d8d82a", "source_hash": "444ced3c687aed2327164a91e0920b8ff34298d03e5257c0da219b15621cb857", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "75da239936000b855d38bf7b3e702b6a569be77b0237c6436930b450ac93164f", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goa